From: OpenWrt RT-AC1200G+ port
Subject: [PATCH] b43: add 2 GHz EPA TX gain table for N-PHY rev 17 / radio 2057 rev 14

BCM43217 boards with an external 2.4 GHz PA (extpagain2g=3, e.g. ASUS
RT-AC1200G+) hit "No 2GHz EPA gain table available for this device": no TX
gain table is uploaded and the radio transmits far below target power.

The table comes from the vendor wl driver: wlc_phy_get_epa_gaintbl_nphy()
selects it for phy_rev 17 on chip 43217 in the 2 GHz band.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_nphy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_nphy.c
@@ -2787,6 +2787,43 @@
 	0x500f0015, 0x500f0015, 0x500f0015, 0x500f0015,
 };
 
+/* BCM43217 (N-PHY rev 17, radio 2057 rev 14) 2 GHz EPA TX gain table.
+ * From the ASUS RT-AC1200G+ stock wl.ko (Asuswrt 3.0.0.4.382_52272). */
